{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"0196fdc6d654352918216407759fbd3867e9f7a09b0ca34b5b31bf2515961118","digest":{"component_or_area":"config schema, code-health subsystem","key_entities":["CodeHealthConfig.enabled","src/rebar/_config_schema.py","src/rebar/_commands/metrics.py","REBAR_CODE_HEALTH_ENABLED","code_health.enabled","src/rebar/_deprecations.py","_SECTIONS","module_size_distribution","oversized_module_count","complexity_summary","duplication_summary"],"problem_keywords":["inert config field","code health analysis","config field never read","structural metrics","config schema"],"propositions":["CodeHealthConfig.enabled field is declared in the schema but has zero read sites in src/rebar, making it inert and unable to gate structural metric evaluation","operator ruled to REMOVE CodeHealthConfig.enabled field rather than wire it to gate metrics, consistent with the dce2 ruling on inert analyzers field","removal requires adding warn-class tombstones for both cfg (code_health.enabled) and env (REBAR_CODE_HEALTH_ENABLED) inputs so that stale configs warn and exit cleanly instead of silently dropping the key","the inert-config gate cannot detect this field because .enabled is read on other configs (ui.enabled, LangfuseConfig), causing it to pass without ever being read itself","documentation falsely advertised an off-switch for code-health analysis that did not actually exist"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787768465910091001,"uuid":"e7e369c2-127f-45a7-8978-6d1aefa7d156"}